// graph: typed graph; sel: selectCorridor result; params: weights (rider profile)
// Options:
//   via            true: route through every waypoint in order; an array: through those waypoint indices (pinned
//                  points) in order; else first -> last point only
//   maxDetour      the route may be at most (1 + maxDetour) x the length of the shortest route (per leg; with
//                  params.avoidTunnels, the shortest tunnel-free route when there is one). The best
//                  route is the lowest-resistance path within that limit, found by a Lagrangian search on
//                  cost = (1-l) * length * scale + l * resistance (bisection on l). Infinity = pure lowest resistance.
//   maxMultiplier  avoid road pieces whose multiplier is above this: they cost AVOID_PENALTY x more (UI: unused).
//   avoidTunnels   hard-close road chains with a tunnel (off by default; the UI's "Avoid tunnels" uses the x50 weight).
//   tunnelAlt      with params.avoidTunnels: when the route is much longer than the best route with tunnels allowed
//                  (TUNNEL_ALT below), that route is added to `alternatives` with throughTunnels = true and the main
//                  result gets tunnelAlt = { extraM, tunnelM, index }. Works with via too.
// "Tunnel" means a tunnel that "avoid tunnels" avoids: a run of at least params.tunnelShortM (weights.mjs).
//   alternatives   how many genuinely different alternative routes to look for (single leg only, i.e. via = false).
//                  Via-node method: a forward search from the start and a backward search to the end give, for every
//                  junction v, the best route through v. Candidates are taken in order of cost and accepted only if
//                  their cost is within altStretch x the best, they don't revisit a junction, and at most altSharing
//                  of their length is shared with the best route or any alternative already chosen.
