// What a search needs before it can start: the cost of every arc and of every turn. They depend only on the graph,
// the selection and the weights, so the last set is kept with the selection: a re-route on the same `sel` object for
// another detour limit, pin or turn-cost scale starts at once, and other weights replace it. It costs about 200 bytes
// per road chain while the selection lives (measured: 139 MB for Mitaka -> Fujiyoshida's 691k chains). The graph's
// arrays must not be changed in place between two calls with the same selection.
