// ---- region packs (packs.mjs, CONTRACT §7b): Japan's road network ready-made, one download per region ----
// In Japan the roads come from the region packs that a route's legs (or the box) need. The first time one question
// names them with their sizes; each is then downloaded whole (one at a time), checked against packs.json and kept in
// IndexedDB, and later builds there read it without any request. Without packs.json (a site that does not host the
// packs), outside every pack, after "Not now" or when a download fails, the live builder works from map tiles as
// before, and the status line says so in one line (packs.note).
const packs = { doc: null, failedAt: -Infinity, stored: new Map(), declined: new Set(), loading: new Map(), waiting: 0, note: null };
